# "Whenever one or more other nontoken permanents with a name originally printed in the Arabian Nights expansion are on the
# battlefield, their controllers sacrifice them" (CR 603.8, 701.21a). Bot1 has Kird Ape and a token copy of it (Relm's
# Sketching), Bot2 Camel, the land Oasis and an Ornithopter. As City in a Bottle enters its state trigger triggers, and its
# controllers sacrifice Kird Ape, Camel and Oasis together; the token stays (the 2004-10-04 ruling), as do Ornithopter, the
# Moxen and City in a Bottle itself, whose own name is an Arabian Nights one ("other"). Two turns later Mirrorweave makes
# Bot2's Ornithopter a copy of the Kird Ape token: a nontoken permanent named Kird Ape now (CR 707.2), with no event, in the
# middle of a resolution - the ability triggers again and Bot2 sacrifices it.

